Z||000012||theogre||03-07-2000||05:18 PM||||I can tell you just from the damage description that the insurance company will likely try to total the car. DO NOT allow them to do this if you are repairing the car. If they insist get a lawyer fast.<P>If they total the car they will own it. You may not be able to buy it back. If you do buy it back you will likely have a "salvage" tittle.<P>A salvage tittle means just that. The car has been labled scrap. Once this is done it can be very dificult to put the car back on the road. (depends on your states laws) The car will always carry the salvage marks on it's tittle history.<P>You'll also need to put the car on a frame machine. You need to make sure the thing is still square. Even a tiny bit off can make the car undrivable.||||reg||1
